# Core Execution Engine

This package holds the ingestion, processing, and worker modules. Each stage is one module
with a single job and a `run_x()` entry point, invoked as `python -m core.<stage>`.
Operational state lives in a SQLite control plane; the chunk vectors and metadata live in a
LanceDB data plane. `run_pipeline.sh` orchestrates the stages.

## Layout

- **`config.py`** — `TOPIC` (from the `research-<topic>` folder), storage paths,
  `EMAIL_CONTACT` (env `NEURO_CONTACT_EMAIL`), optional API keys, the `KEYWORD_BLOCKS`
  query set, chunk parameters, the embedding model, and device selection. All paths derive
  from `__file__`.
- **`registry.py`** — the SQLite control plane at paper grain. `papers` and `cursors`
  tables, the status FSM (`discovered`, `fetched`, `extracted`, `chunked`, `embedded`,
  `paywalled`, `empty`, `duplicate`, `failed`), atomic upserts that preserve `created_at`,
  canonical-DOI / normalized-title / content-hash dedup, and per-source pagination cursors
  stored as opaque JSON.
- **`log.py`** — logging setup (console + `storage/pipeline.log`).
- **`sources/`** — discovery and resolution.
  - `openalex.py`, `europepmc.py`, `crossref.py`: each exposes `discover(block, query,
    cursor, per_page)` yielding normalized paper records and the next pagination cursor.
  - `resolvers.py`: the shared candidate cascade — direct arXiv/PMC/OA links plus the
    Unpaywall / Semantic Scholar / CORE fallbacks — applied to every discovered paper.
- **`ingest.py`** — orchestrates discovery across sources and query blocks: dedups against
  the registry, resolves an open-access URL, fetches a PDF or scrapes HTML to Markdown, and
  registers each paper. Re-resolves a `paywalled` paper when a later source offers an OA
  candidate.
- **`extract.py`** — PDF → Markdown. Runs fitz across processes; escalates to Marker's
  vision model only when fitz quality is low and Marker is installed. Marks a paper
  `duplicate` when its full text hashes to one already extracted.
- **`chunk.py`** — splits Markdown into section-aware, metadata-rich chunks (one JSON per
  paper).
- **`encoders.py`** — the `bge-m3` text encoder: lazy-loaded, batched, L2-normalized, CUDA
  when available. Pluggable so a biomedical embedder can be swapped in later.
- **`embed.py`** — batch-encodes every chunk and upserts one row per chunk into LanceDB.
- **`store.py`** — LanceDB access: the chunk table schema, idempotent upsert by `chunk_id`,
  vector search (the RAG entry point), and Parquet export.
- **`report.py`** — QC statistics over the registry (counts per status, source, query
  block, extraction engine, and total chunks).
- **`purge.py`** — frees disk space by clearing raw PDFs of validated papers only, with
  `--min-quality` retention for future reprocessing.

**Rule**: all modules resolve paths from `__file__` (via `config.py`) so they stay
deployment-agnostic.
